### Dated frontier scan (2026-10-23)

An arXiv API search was run on 2026-10-23. Only metadata and abstracts were
read; no full text, peer review, proof or independent priority check was done.
It gives useful *candidate* frontier updates, not accepted results:

- Omar Kidwai and Guillaume Tahar, “Spectral networks, finite webs, and the
  `T_3` cubic differential,” arXiv:2610.23752v1, submitted 2026-10-16,
  `https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23752v1`. The abstract claims a precise finite-web
  definition and results for one cubic differential on `P^1` with three
  double poles. Full-text review is needed before using any theorem or its
  physical dictionary.
- “Refined Vafa–Witten invariants for toric surfaces from supersymmetric
  localization in 5D gauge theory,” arXiv:2607.18410v1, submitted 2026-07-20,
  `https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18410v1`. The abstract says the relation of its
  even-first-Chern-class partition function to rational refined Vafa–Witten
  invariants remains unclear. Treat that as the authors' preprint status, not
  a community-wide resolution.
- “Localizing the M-Theory Path Integral,” arXiv:2609.31829v2, abstract
  updated 2026-10-07, `https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.31829v2`. The authors call
  their formula a proposal for the local perturbative contribution. It does
  not justify a general rigorous continuum path integral in this library.
- GMN's own 2013 open-problem list remains a guide to questions whose later
  resolution must be checked: D/E-type networks, correct charge quotient,
  higher-rank spectrum generators, refined spin/categorified indices,
  convergence without defects, and cluster-coordinate status. The 2026 `T_3`
  abstract is relevant new evidence for one restricted higher-rank example,
  not evidence that those general questions have all been resolved.

For a genuine `op-` item, first formulate one exact question, inspect the
current full-text literature/status, separate already proved partial results,
and make the open item non-load-bearing. If literature establishes the result
but no local proof exists, record a proof-authoring obligation rather than an
open problem.

## Suggested dependency order and proof/formality ledger

1. Reuse the precise differential-geometric, gauge, characteristic-class and
   finite-regulator pages above. Add local Borel/Cartan cohomology, Borel
   localization, the fixed-component integration formula and equivariant
   index character. Resolve the existing Dirac supplier status before using
   its formula in any dependency closure.
2. Define the named rigid background and off-shell fields, solve its actual
   Killing-spinor equations, define `Q` and compute `Q^2`. Reuse the local
   BRST/anomaly interfaces only to the extent their Abelian setting matches;
   otherwise author a non-Abelian gauge-fixing and anomaly cancellation
   argument with its own hypotheses.
3. For finite regulators, define measure/cycle and prove the Q-Ward identity,
   deformation invariance, zero-mode/stabilizer handling and determinant
   normalization. A claim at this step can be a locally proved finite-model
   result if its regulator actually preserves the chosen symmetry.
4. Record S3/S4 formulas as source-reported conditional field-theory
   calculations until the functional measure and continuum passage are
   justified. For S4 include both instanton and anti-instanton pole sectors;
   for S3 state the exact matter, R-charge and level data.
5. For instantons, prove the fixed-dimensional ADHM/quiver data, torus weights
   and appropriate equivariant pushforward under a precise compactification
   or regulator. Do not call the resulting formal `q`-series a convergent
   partition function without a separate proof.
6. Build classical soliton/monopole claims from a fully specified action,
   boundary conditions and topological charge. Build quantum BPS claims only
   from the sibling's exact algebra/central-charge supplier and a defined
   protected Hilbert-space index.
7. Reuse the finite-field Hall/HN theorem and the CY3 bridge contract as
   mathematical/algebraic context. Any physical DT/BPS identity, all-regime
   chamber spectrum, refined index, or spectral-network reconstruction needs
   its own model-specific proof or a dated, source-reviewed open-problem
   record.

Classify claims as: **proved finite-dimensional mathematics** (for example,
the exact hypotheses of Borel localization once locally proved), **proved
model-conditional physics** (for example, the monopole energy bound from the
stated classical action), **formal/source-reported field-theory derivation**
(S3/S4 and instanton path-integral formulas), or **open/status-pending** (only
after the exact question and literature status are reviewed). No infinite-
dimensional continuum measure, universal localization identity, general
physical BPS count, or all-regime quiver/spectral-network claim is established
by this note.

